{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "ISRM_base",
    "description": "The geometry-independent half of the InMAP ISRM source-receptor model, as a TEMPLATE-LIBRARY file (esm-spec 9.7.1): the expression fragments every emission geometry shares \u2014 the Lambert-conformal forward projection, the cell-containment indicator, the layer-major meteorology gather, the source-receptor contraction term, the ug/m3 scaling and the log-linear concentration-response function. A consuming document (isrm_point.esm, and the polygon / line siblings) imports this file, declares its own variables, equations and data_sources, and spells the shared math as apply_expression_template call sites. WHY A LIBRARY AND NOT A MOUNTED SUBSYSTEM: a library file may not declare models or data_sources (9.7.1), so those are duplicated per consumer \u2014 but the projection-pushdown desugar reads ONE model's own variables and observeds, before flattening (pushdown_rewrite.jl _pd_detect, simulate.jl prepare). Split the SR arrays or the binning aggregates behind a component boundary and the rewrite stops recognising the pattern, the derived support set is never built, and the SR fetch goes from 1520 source rows to the whole 52411-row matrix. Templates are safe where a subsystem is not: detection expands apply_expression_template references before matching, and emission edits the CALL SITE's bindings, never the shared body (conformance fixture pushdown/template_body).",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML"
    ],
    "license": "MIT",
    "created": "2026-08-21T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "isrm",
      "inmap",
      "source_receptor",
      "library",
      "grid",
      "projection",
      "health_impact"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Tessum, C.W., Hill, J.D., Marshall, J.D. (2017). InMAP: A model for air pollution interventions. PLoS ONE 12(4): e0176131.",
        "doi": "10.1371/journal.pone.0176131"
      },
      {
        "citation": "InMAP ISRM tutorial (2022-12-15).",
        "url": "https://inmap.run/blog/2022/12/15/tutorial/"
      }
    ],
    "x_esd": {
      "note": "THE CONTRACT WITH A CONSUMING DOCUMENT. This file owns eleven templates and nothing else. It does NOT own the data_sources, the variable declarations, or any aggregate WRAPPER \u2014 9.7.1 forbids the first two, and the third is a runtime constraint: the projection-pushdown rewrite re-points a matched aggregate's own `ranges`/`args`/`shape`/`join` in place, so those must be authored at the call site; only the aggregate's `expr` BODY may be a template (conformance fixture pushdown/template_body). It also does not own the AXES. A library may carry `index_sets` and `metaparameters` (9.7.5 / 9.7.6), but two consumers read those out of the RAW JSON before 9.7 resolution \u2014 the esio bridge's providers_from_document, which folds a loader select's `range.stop: \"N_SRC\"` while building providers, and the pushdown prepass \u2014 so src_cells / rcv_cells / all_cells / emis_layer / pathways and their sizing metaparameters stay declared in each consuming document. Template bodies name variables this file does not declare: the CRS constants (lat_0/lat_1/lat_2/lon_0/lcc_R/lcc_d2r/lcc_qp), the metaparameter N_SRC, the unit factor `fact`, and TotalPop / MortalityRate / pop_scale / mort_scale. Those are free names resolved in the consuming document; an importer that spells them differently rebinds them at the import edge (9.7.7 `rebind`) rather than editing this file. The index symbols `c`, `r`, `s` and `rcv` are LITERAL in the bodies: a call site must bind them as its aggregate's range keys with exactly these names."
    }
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "cell_contains_point": {
      "description": "1.0 when the record's projected point (ptx, pty) at index r falls in cell c's rectangle [xmin, xmax) x [ymin, ymax), else 0.0. Half-open on the upper edges so a point on a shared boundary lands in exactly one cell. This is the containment the projection-pushdown recogniser reads off a binning aggregate (CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.5.6) \u2014 it must stay a conjunction of comparisons between a cell-indexed bound and a record-indexed coordinate.",
      "params": [
        "xmin",
        "ymin",
        "xmax",
        "ymax",
        "ptx",
        "pty"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "and",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "<=",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "xmin",
                      "c"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "ptx",
                      "r"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "<",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "ptx",
                      "r"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "xmax",
                      "c"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "<=",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "ymin",
                      "c"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "pty",
                      "r"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "<",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "pty",
                      "r"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "ymax",
                      "c"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          1.0,
          0.0
        ]
      }
    },
    "lcc_cone_n": {
      "description": "The Lambert-conformal cone constant for the InMAP grid's CRS, log(cos(lat_1)/cos(lat_2)) / log(tan(qp+lat_2/2)/tan(qp+lat_1/2)). Zero parameters: it depends only on the standard parallels, which the consuming document declares as lat_1 / lat_2 / lcc_qp / lcc_d2r.",
      "params": [],
      "body": {
        "args": [
          {
            "args": [
              {
                "args": [
                  {
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "args": [
                          "lat_1",
                          "lcc_d2r"
                        ],
                        "op": "*"
                      }
                    ],
                    "op": "cos"
                  },
                  {
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "args": [
                          "lat_2",
                          "lcc_d2r"
                        ],
                        "op": "*"
                      }
                    ],
                    "op": "cos"
                  }
                ],
                "op": "/"
              }
            ],
            "op": "log"
          },
          {
            "args": [
              {
                "args": [
                  {
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "args": [
                          "lcc_qp",
                          {
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "args": [
                                  "lat_2",
                                  "lcc_d2r"
                                ],
                                "op": "*"
                              },
                              2.0
                            ],
                            "op": "/"
                          }
                        ],
                        "op": "+"
                      }
                    ],
                    "op": "tan"
                  },
                  {
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "args": [
                          "lcc_qp",
                          {
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "args": [
                                  "lat_1",
                                  "lcc_d2r"
                                ],
                                "op": "*"
                              },
                              2.0
                            ],
                            "op": "/"
                          }
                        ],
                        "op": "+"
                      }
                    ],
                    "op": "tan"
                  }
                ],
                "op": "/"
              }
            ],
            "op": "log"
          }
        ],
        "op": "/"
      }
    },
    "lcc_forward_x": {
      "description": "Lambert-conformal forward projection, easting. `lon` and `lat` are degree-valued expressions. Free names are the CRS constants the consuming document declares: lat_0/lat_1/lat_2/lon_0/lcc_R/lcc_d2r/lcc_qp.",
      "params": [
        "lon",
        "lat"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "lcc_R",
                  {
                    "op": "/",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "cos",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "*",
                                "args": [
                                  "lat_1",
                                  "lcc_d2r"
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "op": "^",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "tan",
                                "args": [
                                  {
                                    "op": "+",
                                    "args": [
                                      "lcc_qp",
                                      {
                                        "op": "/",
                                        "args": [
                                          {
                                            "op": "*",
                                            "args": [
                                              "lat_1",
                                              "lcc_d2r"
                                            ]
                                          },
                                          2.0
                                        ]
                                      }
                                    ]
                                  }
                                ]
                              },
                              {
                                "op": "apply_expression_template",
                                "args": [],
                                "name": "lcc_cone_n",
                                "bindings": {}
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "op": "apply_expression_template",
                        "args": [],
                        "name": "lcc_cone_n",
                        "bindings": {}
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "^",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "tan",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "+",
                        "args": [
                          "lcc_qp",
                          {
                            "op": "/",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "*",
                                "args": [
                                  "lat",
                                  "lcc_d2r"
                                ]
                              },
                              2.0
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "lcc_cone_n",
                    "bindings": {}
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "sin",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "lcc_cone_n",
                    "bindings": {}
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "-",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          "lon",
                          "lcc_d2r"
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          "lon_0",
                          "lcc_d2r"
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "lcc_forward_y": {
      "description": "Lambert-conformal forward projection, northing. See lcc_forward_x.",
      "params": [
        "lon",
        "lat"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "lcc_R",
                  {
                    "op": "/",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "cos",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "*",
                                "args": [
                                  "lat_1",
                                  "lcc_d2r"
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "op": "^",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "tan",
                                "args": [
                                  {
                                    "op": "+",
                                    "args": [
                                      "lcc_qp",
                                      {
                                        "op": "/",
                                        "args": [
                                          {
                                            "op": "*",
                                            "args": [
                                              "lat_1",
                                              "lcc_d2r"
                                            ]
                                          },
                                          2.0
                                        ]
                                      }
                                    ]
                                  }
                                ]
                              },
                              {
                                "op": "apply_expression_template",
                                "args": [],
                                "name": "lcc_cone_n",
                                "bindings": {}
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "op": "apply_expression_template",
                        "args": [],
                        "name": "lcc_cone_n",
                        "bindings": {}
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "^",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "tan",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "+",
                        "args": [
                          "lcc_qp",
                          {
                            "op": "/",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "*",
